Architecture plan for Issue #220: Use the hosted Ideavibes logo URL

Scope and module structure
- Template layer: update the shared public branding in rust-backend/templates/partials/header.html and rust-backend/templates/partials/footer.html so both render the hosted Ideavibes logo image exactly as specified by the issue.
- Domain/content defaults: update rust-backend/src/posts/mod.rs so DEFAULT_COMPANY_LOGO_URL points to https://ideavibes.ai/logo.png for legacy/company-card fallback rendering.
- Test layer: update Rust HTML/template tests in rust-backend/src/html/mod.rs that currently assert committed SVG paths so they assert src="https://ideavibes.ai/logo.png" instead.
- Product documentation: update PRODUCT.md to stop saying header/footer use committed /images/ideavibes-wordmark.svg and document the hosted logo URL instead.

Dependencies between issues
- There is only one issue in this batch. It has no dependencies and can be implemented directly.
- The issue supersedes earlier generated/committed logo asset assumptions; no asset generation or SVG replacement should be performed.

Key design decisions
- Use the product brand/name exactly from the issue: Ideavibes.
- Do not regenerate, modify, or delete favicon assets; the sail-only favicon remains as-is.
- Keep existing static public image serving in place for other committed assets, but stop referencing the old self-generated wordmark SVG for the main brand logo and company fallback.
- Prefer minimal, localized edits in the named files, then run the existing Rust/backend tests and build checks.
